  "assertions": [
    "Origin-zero work preserves an enclosing execution scope after a throw; existing logic passed, so no speculative zero-ID fix was made.",
    "Wrapper identities are captured at encode time and retained under a fixed traced holder that publishes growing list headers.",
    "JSON sorting differs from root insertion order; matching uses captured identity, type and generation.",
    "A transferred host wrapper cannot be re-encoded, but its saved identity remains available.",
    "Actual wrapper movement, all 65 matching aliases released, full collection reclaims that wrapper while preserving a different owner.",
    "Synchronous and async call arguments and import results read only selected WIT record fields and tagged payloads; void results are ignored.",
    "An unselected getter demonstrably throws under the untyped fixture but is skipped by typed encoding; a selected getter collects and preserves its original thrown object.",
    "Pending async imports retain their result schema in private traced slot 24."
  ],
